---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/global.css';
import '../../styles/marketing-pages.css';

const insightsHref = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/+$/, '') + '/insights/';
const steps = [
  ['01', 'Idea and P-paper', 'State the problem, design tradeoffs, examples, implementation experience, and proposed standard wording.'],
  ['02', 'Study and evolution', 'A study group may incubate a proposal. EWG or LEWG discusses language or library design and can request revisions.'],
  ['03', 'Wording review', 'CWG or LWG verifies normative language, consistency, and implementability; insufficiently precise text returns for work.'],
  ['04', 'WG21 plenary', 'Accepted motions add wording to the working draft; papers may instead be revised, deferred, or rejected.'],
  ['05', 'National-body review', 'ISO/IEC Committee Draft (CD) consultation gathers national comments; WG21 addresses issues.'],
  ['06', 'DIS ballot and publication', 'National bodies vote on the Draft International Standard. ISO/IEC applies approval, any required final steps, and publication.'],
];
const takeaways = [
  ['Follow the P-paper revision', 'Votes in a subgroup, plenary adoption and an international ISO ballot are not the same milestone.'],
  ['Account for iteration', 'A paper may loop through revisions after study, evolution, wording, plenary or national comments.'],
  ['Separate paper from product', 'A finalized draft does not mean GCC, Clang and MSVC all implement a feature the same way.'],
  ['Plan real migrations', 'Reflection, contracts, library hardening and std::execution affect tooling, testing and deployment decisions.'],
];
const refs = [
  ['ISO/IEC DIS 14882 status', 'https://www.iso.org/standard/91179.html'],
  ['International C++ working group WG21', 'https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg21/'],
  ['WG21 organization and stages', 'https://isocpp.org/std/the-committee'],
  ['INCITS/C++: U.S. technical advisory group', 'https://www.incits.org/committees/pl22.16'],
  ['ANSI: U.S. representation in ISO', 'https://ansi.org/iso/us-representation-in-iso/introduction'],
  ['ISO/IEC JTC 1/SC 22', 'https://www.iso.org/committee/45202.html'],
  ['March 2026 C++26 committee report', 'https://herbsutter.com/2026/03/29/c26-is-done-trip-report-march-2026-iso-c-standards-meeting-london-croydon-uk/'],
];
---

<BaseLayout title="How C++26 becomes an ISO standard" description="How C++26 moves through WG21, INCITS/C++, ANSI, ISO/IEC review and international approval ballots.">
  <article class="insight-article">
    <header class="article-hero section--hero bg-grid bg-radial">
      <div class="container article-width">
        <a href={insightsHref} class="backlink">&larr; All insights</a>
        <p class="eyebrow">Engineering insights / Standards / C++</p>
        <h1>How C++26 becomes an <span class="gradient-text">ISO standard</span></h1>
        <p class="lede">An idea does not become standardized C++ just because a compiler implements it. Here is the path from a proposal and committee review to an internationally approved language standard.</p>
        <p class="byline"><time datetime="2026-10-16">October 16, 2026</time> · 9-minute read</p>
        <aside class="status">
          <strong>C++26 status on October 16, 2026</strong>
          <p>WG21 completed technical work in March 2026. The new ISO/IEC 14882 edition was at <strong>DIS ballot stage 40.20</strong>, begun July 31, 2026—not yet a published International Standard. <a href="https://www.iso.org/standard/91179.html">Check the live ISO status &nearr;</a></p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="container article-width article-body">
      <section aria-labelledby="people">
        <p class="eyebrow">The organizations</p>
        <h2 id="people">Who writes C++? Who approves it?</h2>
        <p>The international language specification is <strong>ISO/IEC 14882</strong>, developed through ISO/IEC JTC 1, SC 22, WG21. <strong>ANSI</strong> represents the United States at ISO. <strong>INCITS/C++</strong> (formerly PL22.16) is the U.S. Technical Advisory Group (TAG) to WG21. They are connected but distinct.</p>
        <figure class="graph" aria-labelledby="graph-title">
          <h3 id="graph-title">Technical development and national-body governance</h3>
          <div class="branches">
            <div class="branch">
              <span class="branch-label">International technical path</span>
              <div class="node"><strong>Experts + P-papers</strong><small>Research, designs, proposals</small></div>
              <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
              <div class="node node--emphasis"><strong>WG21</strong><small>Study · Evolution · Wording · Plenary</small></div>
              <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
              <div class="node"><strong>Working draft</strong><small>ISO/IEC 14882 text</small></div>
            </div>
            <div class="branch">
              <span class="branch-label">U.S. national-body path</span>
              <div class="node"><strong>U.S. stakeholders</strong><small>Engineers, organizations, experts</small></div>
              <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
              <div class="node node--emphasis"><strong>INCITS/C++</strong><small>U.S. consensus and advisory group</small></div>
              <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
              <div class="node"><strong>ANSI</strong><small>U.S. member body of ISO</small></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="join" aria-hidden="true">↘ &nbsp; ISO national-body review and ballots &nbsp; ↙</div>
          <div class="node node--outcome"><strong>ISO/IEC 14882</strong><small>Published International Standard, after approval</small></div>
          <figcaption>International experts develop the working draft; national standards bodies including ANSI provide formal national positions and ballot votes. Simplified relationship graph, not an organization chart.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p><strong>What about “ANSI C++”?</strong> This is historical shorthand, not a second C++26 technical design committee. ANSI coordinates U.S. participation and positions. A separate American National Standard or national adoption designation, if applicable, is not the same as approval of features by WG21.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="pipeline">
        <p class="eyebrow">A proposal is a process, not a switch</p>
        <h2 id="pipeline">The C++ approval pipeline</h2>
        <figure class="graph">
          <ol class="pipeline">
            {steps.map(([number, title, detail]) => (
              <li><span class="stepnum">{number}</span><div class="step"><h3>{title}</h3><p>{detail}</p></div></li>
            ))}
          </ol>
          <p class="loop"><strong>Revision loop:</strong> A failed consensus check, wording problem, committee decision, or national comment can return a proposal to earlier stages. A study group is not mandatory for every proposal.</p>
          <figcaption>Pipeline graphic. See the <a href="https://github.com/canonical-cloud/canonical-marketing-site.web/blob/main/docs/insights/cpp26-standardization.md">Markdown/Mermaid source</a> for explicit decision diamonds, alternate paths, and a U.S. governance graph.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="decision-grid">
          <div><h3>EWG / LEWG</h3><p>Design consensus: advance, revise or defer a language/library feature.</p></div>
          <div><h3>CWG / LWG</h3><p>Normative wording, defects, compatibility and integration into the draft.</p></div>
          <div><h3>WG21 plenary</h3><p>Motions adopt technical wording. That is not the final ISO publication vote.</p></div>
          <div><h3>ISO / IEC national bodies</h3><p>CD comments and DIS ballots; additional editorial or FDIS steps as applicable.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="status-cpp">
        <p class="eyebrow">The C++26 example</p>
        <h2 id="status-cpp">“C++26 is done” is not “ISO has published it”</h2>
        <p>WG21 finished the C++26 technical feature set in March 2026, including major work on <strong>compile-time reflection</strong>, <strong>contracts</strong>, <strong>standard-library hardening</strong> and <code>std::execution</code>. The international standards lifecycle continues separately.</p>
        <div class="timeline">
          <div><time datetime="2025-08">Aug 2025</time><strong>Committee Draft review</strong><p>International CD consultation starts.</p></div>
          <div><time datetime="2026-03">Mar 2026</time><strong>Technical completion</strong><p>WG21 finalizes the feature set.</p></div>
          <div><time datetime="2026-07-31">Jul 31, 2026</time><strong>DIS ballot starts</strong><p>ISO stage 40.20: 12 weeks.</p></div>
          <div><span>Later</span><strong>Approval and publication</strong><p>Pending formal ISO/IEC process, not yet published as of this article.</p></div>
        </div>
        <p>The most recent <em>published</em> C++ edition on this date is ISO/IEC 14882:2024 (C++23). After ISO publication, teams still need to verify compiler versions, feature availability and the migration risks of adopting C++26.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="takeaways">
        <p class="eyebrow">Insights</p>
        <h2 id="takeaways">What engineering teams should take away</h2>
        <div class="decision-grid">
          {takeaways.map(([heading, detail]) => <div><h3>{heading}</h3><p>{detail}</p></div>)}
        </div>
        <p class="disclaimer">A programming-language standard is not a certification of a cloud provider, software product, or organization. Standardization and compliance assurance are different processes.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="sources">
        <h2 id="sources">Primary sources</h2>
        <ul class="references">
          {refs.map(([label, url]) => <li><a href={url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{label} &nearr;</a></li>)}
        </ul>
        <p class="disclaimer">Independent editorial explanation. Not an official statement on behalf of ISO, IEC, WG21, ANSI, or INCITS. Status is current to the publication date; consult the source links for updates.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
  <style>
    .article-width{max-width:940px}.article-hero{padding-bottom:var(--space-3xl)}.backlink,.article-body a{color:var(--av-emerald);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}.backlink{display:inline-block;margin-bottom:var(--space-lg)}.eyebrow{color:var(--av-teal);font-size:.78rem;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.13em}.article-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.5rem,5vw,4.5rem);line-height:1.08;margin:1rem 0}.lede{font-size:clamp(1.06rem,2vw,1.32rem);max-width:800px;color:var(--av-text-secondary);line-height:1.7}.byline{margin:1.3rem 0;color:var(--av-text-muted);font-size:.86rem}.status{margin-top:1.8rem;border-left:4px solid var(--av-emerald);border-radius:var(--radius-sm);background:var(--av-emerald-glow);padding:1.25rem}.status p{margin-top:.4rem}.status a{color:var(--av-emerald);text-decoration:underline}.article-body{padding-bottom:var(--space-4xl)}.article-body section{padding-top:var(--space-2xl)}.article-body section+section{margin-top:var(--space-3xl);border-top:1px solid var(--av-border)}.article-body h2{font-size:clamp(1.7rem,3vw,2.35rem);margin:.6rem 0 1.1rem}.article-body section>p{line-height:1.8;color:var(--av-text-secondary);margin-bottom:1.2rem}.graph{padding:var(--space-lg);background:var(--av-surface);border:1px solid var(--av-border);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);margin:1.6rem 0}.graph>h3{font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:1.1rem}.branches{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.branch{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:.25rem;min-width:0}.branch-label{font-size:.75rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--av-teal);text-align:center;min-height:2rem}.node{width:100%;padding:1rem .6rem;border:1px solid var(--av-border-active);background:var(--av-surface-elevated);border-radius:var(--radius-md);text-align:center}.node strong,.node small{display:block}.node small{color:var(--av-text-secondary);font-size:.78rem;margin-top:.4rem}.node--emphasis{border-color:var(--av-emerald)}.node--outcome{border:2px solid var(--av-emerald);background:var(--av-emerald-glow)}.arrow{font-size:1.4rem;color:var(--av-emerald);font-weight:800}.join{text-align:center;color:var(--av-teal);font-size:.82rem;font-weight:800;margin:1rem 0 .5rem}figcaption{color:var(--av-text-muted);font-size:.83rem;line-height:1.6;margin-top:1rem}.pipeline{display:grid;gap:.85rem;list-style:none;padding:0}.pipeline li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:3rem minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem;position:relative}.pipeline li:not(:last-child)::after{content:'↓';position:absolute;left:.9rem;bottom:-.95rem;color:var(--av-emerald);font-weight:800}.stepnum{background:var(--av-emerald-glow);border:1px solid var(--av-border-active);border-radius:var(--radius-md);padding:.8rem 0;text-align:center;color:var(--av-emerald);font-weight:800;align-self:start}.step{background:var(--av-surface-elevated);border:1px solid var(--av-border);border-radius:var(--radius-md);padding:.8rem 1rem}.step h3{font-size:1.02rem;margin-bottom:.3rem}.step p,.decision-grid p,.timeline p{color:var(--av-text-secondary);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6}.loop{border-left:3px solid var(--av-warning);background:var(--av-warning-glow);padding:1rem;margin-top:1rem;font-size:.92rem}.decision-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem;margin:1.5rem 0}.decision-grid>div{background:var(--av-surface);border:1px solid var(--av-border);border-radius:var(--radius-md);padding:1.2rem}.decision-grid h3{font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:.4rem}.timeline{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.75rem;margin:1.5rem 0}.timeline>div{background:var(--av-surface);border-top:3px solid var(--av-emerald);padding:1rem;border-radius:var(--radius-sm)}.timeline strong{display:block;margin-bottom:.4rem}.timeline time,.timeline span{display:block;color:var(--av-teal);font-size:.78rem;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:.75rem}.references{list-style:disc;padding-left:1.4rem}.references li{margin:.7rem 0}.disclaimer{border-left:3px solid var(--av-warning);padding:1rem;background:var(--av-warning-glow);font-size:.87rem}@media(max-width:750px){.branches,.decision-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.timeline{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:480px){.timeline{grid-template-columns:1fr}.graph{padding:.8rem}}
  </style>
</BaseLayout>